WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.179
Your next-intl messages
are already ICU,

2
00:00:04.179 --> 00:00:06.674
so most components
change only imports.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:10.610
General Translation's gt-next
keeps your messages while you

4
00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:11.805
move copy inline.

5
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.031
Swap next-intl's plugin,

6
00:00:15.031 --> 00:00:18.130
middleware, and
provider for gt-next's.

7
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.597
Load messages/en.json
as a dictionary,

8
00:00:22.597 --> 00:00:25.360
and match next-intl's
locale prefix setting.

9
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:30.864
Add loadDictionary.ts at the
project root to load your existing

10
00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:31.861
translations.

11
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.762
The config covers standard prefixes,

12
00:00:35.762 --> 00:00:39.697
so map localized pathnames before
removing next-intl's routing.

13
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:43.157
Then move copy into the T component,

14
00:00:43.157 --> 00:00:44.363
one route at a time.

15
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:49.817
Run npx gt translate with the
dictionary flag while you keep

16
00:00:49.817 --> 00:00:50.524
the catalog.

17
00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.494
Your team now ships
German with each release.
